{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "00281",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 0.65,
      "end_seconds": 3.25,
      "duration_seconds": 2.6,
      "text": "Okay, welcome. Let's see what's going on."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 4.64,
      "end_seconds": 6.5,
      "duration_seconds": 1.86,
      "text": "Hello, doctor, thank you."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 7.36,
      "end_seconds": 12.83,
      "duration_seconds": 5.47,
      "text": "Oh, hello, doctor, I came in with them, if that's okay."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 13.52,
      "end_seconds": 17.38,
      "duration_seconds": 3.86,
      "text": "Absolutely, come and sit beside them. Okay. Start wherever you like."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 18.42,
      "end_seconds": 25.93,
      "duration_seconds": 7.51,
      "text": "Well, I've been having yellow eyes. I just want to get back to normal, really."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 27.48,
      "end_seconds": 30.9,
      "duration_seconds": 3.42,
      "text": "Okay, anything that tends to go along with it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 32.32,
      "end_seconds": 39.52,
      "duration_seconds": 7.2,
      "text": "A dull ache on the right side of the tummy goes along with it, most of the time."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 40.11,
      "end_seconds": 47.17,
      "duration_seconds": 7.06,
      "text": "Hmm, and the other thing I wanted to mention is that I can't really—"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 47.27,
      "end_seconds": 53.33,
      "duration_seconds": 6.06,
      "text": "Uh, tell the doctor about the other thing, that's what worries me."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 54.41,
      "end_seconds": 60.78,
      "duration_seconds": 6.37,
      "text": "I was getting to that! I mean, I've also had dark urine, for two days."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 61.62,
      "end_seconds": 65.06,
      "duration_seconds": 3.44,
      "text": "Does it happen all the time or in spells?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 66.58,
      "end_seconds": 72.96,
      "duration_seconds": 6.38,
      "text": "It's, you know, um... not exactly... well, hard to explain, I mean—"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 74.35,
      "end_seconds": 80.05,
      "duration_seconds": 5.7,
      "text": "Let me put it another way: how many times in a typical day or week?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 81.63,
      "end_seconds": 83.5,
      "duration_seconds": 1.87,
      "text": "Honestly, every other day."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 83.8,
      "end_seconds": 85.53,
      "duration_seconds": 1.73,
      "text": "And fever, any of that?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 86.13,
      "end_seconds": 87.55,
      "duration_seconds": 1.42,
      "text": "No. No fever."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 88.95,
      "end_seconds": 93.37,
      "duration_seconds": 4.42,
      "text": "Actually, doctor, I did notice fever. She doesn't always say."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 94.27,
      "end_seconds": 101.18,
      "duration_seconds": 6.91,
      "text": "Right, um, no, I don't think I did. Maybe a little, I'm not sure."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 102.09,
      "end_seconds": 107.87,
      "duration_seconds": 5.78,
      "text": "Alright, I'll note both what you've said and what you've noticed. Any confusion or swelling of the tummy?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 108.88,
      "end_seconds": 118.81,
      "duration_seconds": 9.93,
      "text": "No, no confusion, no swelling of the tummy. I did have itching all over at one point, but that went away on its own."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 120.02,
      "end_seconds": 124.21,
      "duration_seconds": 4.19,
      "text": "Have you had any weight loss, black stools or vomiting blood?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 125.59,
      "end_seconds": 131.12,
      "duration_seconds": 5.53,
      "text": "Yeah, I haven't had weight loss, black stools or vomiting blood, no."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 132.02,
      "end_seconds": 134.36,
      "duration_seconds": 2.34,
      "text": "Any problems with your joints or muscles?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 135.38,
      "end_seconds": 138.56,
      "duration_seconds": 3.18,
      "text": "No, you know, joints are fine."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 139.3,
      "end_seconds": 142.57,
      "duration_seconds": 3.27,
      "text": "Any medication at the moment, including things from the pharmacy?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 143.49,
      "end_seconds": 147.16,
      "duration_seconds": 3.67,
      "text": "I'm on metformin, 500 milligrams, twice a day."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 148.32,
      "end_seconds": 157.26,
      "duration_seconds": 8.94,
      "text": "Doctor, you know, I think the last prescription for the metformin was 250 milligrams. We changed it at the last visit."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 158.44,
      "end_seconds": 161.73,
      "duration_seconds": 3.29,
      "text": "Hm, that's different. Is the latest prescription anywhere near you?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 163.02,
      "end_seconds": 168.38,
      "duration_seconds": 5.36,
      "text": "I mean, uh, I don't think I have it with me."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 169.93,
      "end_seconds": 177.44,
      "duration_seconds": 7.51,
      "text": "It's a... um, uh, I can't remember what it's called. It's a small white one."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 178.14,
      "end_seconds": 180.99,
      "duration_seconds": 2.85,
      "text": "Okay, do you remember what it's for?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 182.18,
      "end_seconds": 190.35,
      "duration_seconds": 8.17,
      "text": "I mean, for my cholesterol, I believe. My wife sets them out for me, I just take what I'm given."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 191.52,
      "end_seconds": 195.23,
      "duration_seconds": 3.71,
      "text": "What about family history, any illnesses that run in the family?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 195.91,
      "end_seconds": 197.85,
      "duration_seconds": 1.94,
      "text": "My brother has asthma."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 198.47,
      "end_seconds": 201.69,
      "duration_seconds": 3.22,
      "text": "Alright, do you have any known allergies at all?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 202.3,
      "end_seconds": 210.73,
      "duration_seconds": 8.43,
      "text": "I mean, yes, peanuts, it gives me my lips swelling. Dust. I come out in... well, itchy eyes."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 211.21,
      "end_seconds": 212.6,
      "duration_seconds": 1.39,
      "text": "And alcohol, how much?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 213.87,
      "end_seconds": 217.16,
      "duration_seconds": 3.29,
      "text": "I gave up drinking about three years ago."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 218.28,
      "end_seconds": 219.38,
      "duration_seconds": 1.1,
      "text": "How about smoking?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 220.68,
      "end_seconds": 223.56,
      "duration_seconds": 2.88,
      "text": "I smoke about ten cigarettes a day."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 224.91,
      "end_seconds": 228.1,
      "duration_seconds": 3.19,
      "text": "Moving on to your background, any past medical history?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 229.69,
      "end_seconds": 237.12,
      "duration_seconds": 7.43,
      "text": "Well, I've had diabetes for about ten years now. I've never really been one for hospitals."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0043",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 238.19,
      "end_seconds": 238.89,
      "duration_seconds": 0.7,
      "text": "Right."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0044",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 240.25,
      "end_seconds": 248.29,
      "duration_seconds": 8.04,
      "text": "Um, I've had high cholesterol for nearly five years now. I'm hoping you can tell me something definite."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0045",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 248.87,
      "end_seconds": 252.06,
      "duration_seconds": 3.19,
      "text": "Let's get your blood pressure and the other basics."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0046",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 260.33,
      "end_seconds": 261.85,
      "duration_seconds": 1.52,
      "text": "Just relax your arm..."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0047",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 281.83,
      "end_seconds": 288.97,
      "duration_seconds": 7.14,
      "text": "Okay: heart rate 73, temperature 36.8. And respiratory rate 14, saturation 98 percent, pressure 108 over 73."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0048",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 291.89,
      "end_seconds": 294.59,
      "duration_seconds": 2.7,
      "text": "Hmm, is that alright, doctor?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0049",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 295.05,
      "end_seconds": 297.7,
      "duration_seconds": 2.65,
      "text": "We'll put it in context in a moment."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0050",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 299.69,
      "end_seconds": 303.77,
      "duration_seconds": 4.08,
      "text": "Alright, I'd like to examine you now. Please come over here."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0051",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 305.3,
      "end_seconds": 306.0,
      "duration_seconds": 0.7,
      "text": "Okay."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0052",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 306.94,
      "end_seconds": 308.88,
      "duration_seconds": 1.94,
      "text": "Hold your arm out like this."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0053",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 320.62,
      "end_seconds": 323.12,
      "duration_seconds": 2.5,
      "text": "Liver edge is just palpable and mildly tender."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0054",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 323.93,
      "end_seconds": 324.63,
      "duration_seconds": 0.7,
      "text": "Hm."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0055",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 326.17,
      "end_seconds": 327.71,
      "duration_seconds": 1.54,
      "text": "Bear with me a second."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0056",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 343.43,
      "end_seconds": 345.68,
      "duration_seconds": 2.25,
      "text": "The whites of your eyes are yellow."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0057",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 346.14,
      "end_seconds": 346.84,
      "duration_seconds": 0.7,
      "text": "Alright."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0058",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 351.65,
      "end_seconds": 373.11,
      "duration_seconds": 21.46,
      "text": "Okay, you can sit back up. Thank you for that. I'll write up what I found in a moment, and then I'll tell you what I think is going on. Okay, so my impression is this: I think we're dealing with jaundice with a cause we still need to find at this stage. I can't rule out a gallstone blocking the bile duct yet."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0059",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 374.43,
      "end_seconds": 376.52,
      "duration_seconds": 2.09,
      "text": "Is it something serious, doctor?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0060",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 376.87,
      "end_seconds": 396.19,
      "duration_seconds": 19.32,
      "text": "I understand the worry. At the moment I'd say it's jaundice with a cause we still need to find, and we'll know more once the liver function tests is back. We should do liver function tests for jaundice. I'd rather check than guess, and this is the quickest way to know more."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0061",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "CLINICAL_STAFF",
      "start_seconds": 397.69,
      "end_seconds": 402.19,
      "duration_seconds": 4.5,
      "text": "We have a slot Tuesday at 11:30 am, if that works."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0062",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 402.86,
      "end_seconds": 410.57,
      "duration_seconds": 7.71,
      "text": "Let's get a hepatitis screen, for jaundice. I'd rather check than guess, and this is the quickest way to know more."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0063",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 411.89,
      "end_seconds": 415.22,
      "duration_seconds": 3.33,
      "text": "Sure, where do I go for that?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0064",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 416.06,
      "end_seconds": 419.95,
      "duration_seconds": 3.89,
      "text": "I'd like to arrange an ultrasound of the abdomen for jaundice."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0065",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 421.06,
      "end_seconds": 422.06,
      "duration_seconds": 1.0,
      "text": "Okay, doctor."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0066",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 422.73,
      "end_seconds": 447.34,
      "duration_seconds": 24.61,
      "text": "Please avoid alcohol completely and don't take any painkillers except paracetamol, and not much of that. Make sure you're drinking plenty of fluids, two to three litres a day if you can, and get proper rest. Cut down on salt and fried food for now, it really does make a difference. I'd like you to see a liver specialist as well, and I'll write the referral."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0067",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 447.69,
      "end_seconds": 455.64,
      "duration_seconds": 7.95,
      "text": "And please bring the latest prescription or the medicine boxes to the next visit, so we can settle the dose."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0068",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 457.1,
      "end_seconds": 458.66,
      "duration_seconds": 1.56,
      "text": "Okay, I will."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0069",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 459.99,
      "end_seconds": 471.51,
      "duration_seconds": 11.52,
      "text": "Keep an eye out, and if you vomit blood or become drowsy or confused, call us the same day or go to emergency. Come back after the results are back."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0070",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 474.39,
      "end_seconds": 477.42,
      "duration_seconds": 3.03,
      "text": "Okay, you know, I'll book that."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0071",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 478.78,
      "end_seconds": 483.03,
      "duration_seconds": 4.25,
      "text": "Good. Call the clinic if you need us in the meantime."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0072",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 483.44,
      "end_seconds": 487.46,
      "duration_seconds": 4.02,
      "text": "Okay, so no, you've explained it well. Thanks."
    }
  ]
}